54349 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754288 1071 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 5](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/5).\n\nFind the general solution to $y''+4y'+29y=0$. Use $c_1,c_2$ for arbitrary constants and $x$ as the independent variable. In WeBWorK enter the full equation $y=\\cdots$, typing the constants as `c1` and `c2`.\n\nEquation: $y=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754288 1072 #uuid "387cde60-2e38-5ca8-95e4-ae8ebaeb094f" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754288 1074 "The characteristic equation is $(r+2)^2+25=0$, with roots $-2\\pm5i$. The real part gives the factor $e^{-2x}$ and the imaginary part gives frequency $5$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754289 1080 "\\frac{e^{3 t}}{10} + \\frac{9 e^{- \\frac{t}{3}}}{10}" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754289 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754289 1083 #uuid "3906dc48-445c-532c-8255-0ece34f75790" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754290 1080 "2 t^{2} - 18 t - \\frac{e^{3 t}}{14} + 66" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754290 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754290 1083 #uuid "3a01456b-f5ea-5c6d-9c36-5388c6cbf969" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754291 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754274 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754291 1071 "Find a particular solution to the nonhomogeneous equation.\n\n$y_p=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754291 1072 #uuid "3af1dc16-4f0d-5d5d-831e-6bfe33a49690" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754291 1074 "The homogeneous root $4$ has multiplicity two, so try $y_p=Ax^2e^{4x}$. Since $(D-4)^2(e^{4x}u)=e^{4x}u''$, substitution gives $2Ae^{4x}=e^{4x}$ and $A=1/2$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754292 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754363 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754292 1071 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 4](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/4).\n\nFind the general solution to $3y''+75y=0$. Use $c_1,c_2$ for arbitrary constants and $x$ as the independent variable. In WeBWorK enter the full equation $y=\\cdots$, typing the constants as `c1` and `c2`.\n\nEquation: $y=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754292 1072 #uuid "3b8205f1-49f5-5f5b-8233-53329f239bfe" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754292 1074 "Dividing by $3$ gives $y''+25y=0$. The roots $r=\\pm5i$ yield the real solution $y=c_1\\cos(5x)+c_2\\sin(5x)$; differentiating twice multiplies either term by $-25$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754293 1080 "\\frac{- 17 \\log{\\left(x \\right)} - 6}{x^{3}}" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754293 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754293 1083 #uuid "3ee69056-7886-52cd-a402-1c8bb054f1a3" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754294 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754340 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754294 1062 #uuid "4066fcdf-cf35-5888-bbc3-6cc398fe8bc8" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754294 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754272 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754295 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754413 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754295 1071 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 15](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/15).\n\nFind a particular solution to $y''+36y=-24\\sin(6t)$.\n\n$y_p(t)=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754295 1072 #uuid "414d7403-ea18-5cc2-87f3-adf188eab803" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754295 1074 "The forcing is resonant with the homogeneous sine/cosine solutions. Since $(D^2+36)[t\\cos(6t)]=-12\\sin(6t)$, multiplying by $2$ gives the required forcing $-24\\sin(6t)$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754296 1068 #edb/ref 17592186