\n\nUse the equation $y''+4y'+5y=-10x+3e^{-x}$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754387 1086 #uuid "d7dbc885-ae7e-5ce6-9128-2775328074d1" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754387 1087 #edb/ref 17592186754319 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754388 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754325 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754388 1071 "**(a)** Find the general solution. Use $c_1,c_2$ for arbitrary constants and $x$ as the independent variable. In WeBWorK enter the full equation $y=\\cdots$, typing the constants as `c1` and `c2`.\n\nEquation: $y=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754388 1072 #uuid "d9256045-2740-5c25-a7df-a01b54fa39c4" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754388 1074 "The characteristic equation is $r(r+7)=0$. The root $0$ contributes the constant solution $e^{0x}=1$; the other root contributes $e^{-7x}$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754389 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754265 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754389 1062 #uuid "d944fd58-169e-572c-84b1-3e252013a431" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754389 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754336 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754390 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754298 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754390 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754390 1077 "solution" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754390 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754298 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754390 1079 #uuid "d9685506-debb-5dbe-a511-c3e80ae86e0f" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754391 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754317 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754391 1071 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 18](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/18).\n\nFind a particular solution to $6y''+5y'+y=2t^2+2t-5e^{3t}$.\n\n$y_p(t)=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754391 1072 #uuid "dc448596-9744-57e6-90a4-9cbde7827d8f" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754391 1074 "Use $y_p=At^2+Bt+C+De^{3t}$. Polynomial coefficients give $A=2$, $10A+B=2$, and $12A+5B+C=0$, hence $B=-18$, $C=66$. The exponential coefficient gives $(54+15+1)D=-5$, so $D=-1/14$. Adding these terms produces the required forcing by linearity." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754392 1080 "c_1 \\cos{\\left(5 x \\right)} + c_2 \\sin{\\left(5 x \\right)}" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754392 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754392 1083 #uuid "e06cad81-48b3-5df8-a15d-a1fb868197ce" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754393 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754400 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754393 1071 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 14](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_4/14).\n\nFind $y(t)$ satisfying $y''+3y'=18\\sin(3t)+54\\cos(3t)$, $y(0)=3$, and $y'(0)=3$.\n\n$y(t)=$ {{solution}}." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754393 1072 #uuid "e0d20620-89eb-5704-a32f-fb2d1d0136ec" 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754393 1074 "The homogeneous solution is $A+Be^{-3t}$. For $y_p=C\\cos(3t)+D\\sin(3t)$, matching cosine and sine coefficients gives $-9C+9D=54$ and $-9C-9D=18$, hence $C=-4$, $D=2$. Then $A+B-4=3$ and $-3B+6=3$, giving $B=1$ and $A=6$." 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048826 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049099 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049832 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050150 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050271 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050895 13194139546555 17592186502323 true] [17592186754394 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754330 13194139546555 17592186502323 true]